  "body": "This extends #2564\u2019s scalar F0\u2192F2 quotient to a **conditional native source-response factorization** for the selected prefix: 11 complete local sweeps, four bridges and four idle sweeps, with centre ablations at calls 0 and 10.\r\n\r\nFor the complete prefix `F`, ablated diagnostic `A`, initial X0 source data `d`, and arbitrary other contents `h` held fixed:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nE_D d = (F-A)(d,h) - (F-A)(0,h)\r\nP_D d = first eight complete native pre-transport centre-field responses to (d,0)\r\n\r\nker(P_D) \u2286 ker(E_D), hence E_D = L_native P_D.\r\n```\r\n\r\nSigned boundary identities cancel the X0 response at B1. At F2, all eight pre-centre rows vanish on the 112 target and 99 helper roles that remain potentially live. The proof compares complete terminal continuations.\r\n\r\nStart with the commit-pinned [proof and scope](https://github.com/DLamdata/integer-mult-bounds/blob/f122d255c4cdb0714c079d8e91b76bd7a34da23e/research/centre-native-terminal-factor/README.md) and [validation record](https://github.com/DLamdata/integer-mult-bounds/blob/f122d255c4cdb0714c079d8e91b76bd7a34da23e/research/centre-native-terminal-factor/VALIDATION.md). Only `research/centre-native-terminal-factor/` changes.\r\n\r\nThe result assumes the declared complete native common-frame and cover/local-view interface. The eight fields include owner, payload and spectator indices. It does not establish sharp native rank eight, recover the dirty offset, supply a paid decoder, rebuild the physical compiler, reduce the invoice or change \u03ba. A fully charged dirty-residual consumer remains open.\r\n\r\n**Local validation**\r\n\r\n- All three registered checks passed in 100.148 seconds on CPython 3.12.14, including exact signed boundary identities and an independently derived reverse-adjoint check.\r\n- The three mathematical checkers also passed with `-I -O -B` in a relocated, read-only export without `.git`. The Git-dependent metadata launcher and committed-byte checker ran separately in the Git checkout. Corruption controls detected altered sources and receipts.\r\n- Committed-byte verification passed for 22 package/input files; all 12 published package blobs matched the reviewed commit. Detailed commands and resolved review findings are in the validation record.\r\n\r\n**Remote CI \u2014 snapshot at 2026-10-16 10:29 UTC**\r\n\r\n[Fork checks](https://github.com/DLamdata/integer-mult-bounds/commit/f122d255c4cdb0714c079d8e91b76bd7a34da23e/checks): **56 successful / 23 failed**. [Upstream PR checks](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2907/checks): **61 queued**.\r\n\r\nAll failed fork jobs were inspected. Observed causes were inherited source/receipt-pin drift, singleton-target unpacking, missing historical Git objects, ledger/digest mismatches and symlink-cycle handling. Exact guards, targeted parent/head reproductions and checkout-history evidence established their presence in integration parent `ba3de472\u2026`. No contribution-related failure was found. Blocked later steps and queued upstream checks remain unverified; no complete CI pass is claimed.\r\n\r\nComparison with upstream `475fec190d5ad746bd4690574dca30d6901acdaf` found scientific pins, relevant guidance and package verification tools unchanged. No rebase or mathematical rerun was warranted. Reviewed head: `f122d255c4cdb0714c079d8e91b76bd7a34da23e`.\r\n\r\nCredit ywz65/#2564, the cited lineage (#2048, #2199, #2391, #2461), and Sagar Thakrar\u2019s unchanged Clifford kernel. Prepared by DLamdata with substantial Codex assistance. The checks share the selected archive/native-view premise; primary and boundary checks share the kernel. AI review is not independent human or formal global verification. New work is Apache-2.0.\r\n\r\n[Canonical Discussion update](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1884#discussioncomment-18967805).",
